    <h2 class="section-title">1. Abstract & Objective</h2>
    <p>The project focuses on building a state-of-the-art cloud-native Serverless Microservices Architecture (SMA) utilizing <span class="bold-text">Java 17</span> and <span class="bold-text">Spring Boot 3</span>. Traditional cloud deployments (e.g., VMs or dedicated containers) run continuously and incur significant costs during idle phases. Serverless architectures solve this with pay-per-invocation billing and auto-scaling. However, the Java runtime faces severe <span class="bold-text">Cold Start</span> delays (often 5 to 10 seconds). The primary objective of this research is to build a reference microservices implementation that completely mitigates Java's cold start latency to less than <span class="bold-text">200 milliseconds</span> and dramatically reduces overall hosting expenses by over <span class="bold-text">85%</span> using targeted cloud structural optimizations.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title">2. Completed Architecture & Optimizations</h2>
    <p>We have modified the traditional serverless setup with four architectural upgrades to maximize cost savings and performance:</p>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="bold-text">CPU Architecture Shift (ARM64):</span> Moved execution runtime from x86_64 to <span class="bold-text">AWS Graviton (arm64)</span> processors, saving 20% on computing bills while increasing execution speed.</li>
        <li><span class="bold-text">API Gateway Optimization (HTTP APIs):</span> Replaced REST API Gateway with <span class="bold-text">HTTP APIs</span>, reducing integration costs by 71% and reducing HTTP routing overhead.</li>
        <li><span class="bold-text">Memory Tuning & Stripping (256MB):</span> Removed default embedded Tomcat server web runtimes and heavy HTTP client pools to run Spring Boot inside 256MB memory without performance loss (50% cheaper execution).</li>
        <li><span class="bold-text">AWS Lambda SnapStart (CRaC Integration):</span> Enabled SnapStart (Coordinated Restore at Checkpoint) configuration. Bypasses standard JVM startup by restoring directly from frozen VM snapshots in under 150ms.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="section-title">3. Current Code Base Structure</h2>
    <p>The repository contains the fully customized project templates ready for local compilation and deployment packages generation:</p>
    <pre>Optimized_Implementation/
+-- template.yaml                          # SAM Infrastructure-as-code (SnapStart/ARM64 configuration)
+-- user-service/                          # Main User Management Service
    +-- pom.xml                            # Lightweight dependency mapping with Tomcat exclusions
    +-- src/main/java/com/cloudresearch/userservice/
        +-- UserServiceApplication.java    # Main entrypoint with DynamoDB configs
        +-- handler/
        ¦   +-- StreamLambdaHandler.java   # CRaC Checkpoint handler hooks
        +-- controller/
        ¦   +-- UserController.java        # REST controllers mapping
        +-- service/
            +-- UserService.java           # Business logic & security algorithms</pre>

    <h2 class="section-title">4. Performance Metrics & Comparative Study</h2>
    <p>Simulated load testing using Apache JMeter (1000 concurrent users, 10 min duration) reveals significant performance improvements:</p>
